---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { modelRelease } from '../../lib/model-pages';
const release = modelRelease(); const cov = release.coverage;
---
<Layout locale="en" title="Data sources, pricing method and evidence — MaaS Daily" description="Understand source observations, original pricing conditions, timestamps, evidence completeness, failed updates, revisions and the limits of price comparisons.">
  <article><h1>How we observe MaaS platforms</h1><p>Data through {release.dataThrough}: {cov.changes.count} change records from {cov.changes.from} to {cov.changes.to}, {cov.prices.facts} pricing facts, {cov.evidence.count} evidence records and {cov.weekly.count} published weekly reports.</p>
    <h2>1. Official sources and observations</h2><p>We periodically fetch official model lists, pricing pages, release notes and blogs, then compare page text with the previous snapshot. Truncation, page movement and recomputation may produce noise. A changed page does not establish an official launch, withdrawal or price adjustment; check the linked official announcement.</p>
    <h2>2. Different timestamps answer different questions</h2><ul><li>observedAt is when our collector saw the content.</li><li>publishedAt is the supplier's stated publication time; it remains empty without a source.</li><li>A pricing fact's observation interval records its version history.</li><li>dataThrough is the dataset coverage boundary, currently {release.dataThrough}.</li><li>A site build time is a publication operation, not evidence of fresh source data.</li></ul><p>Official effective dates are not inferred from observation times.</p>
    <h2>3. Evidence completeness</h2><p>Pricing evidence includes a saved excerpt, a locator and an excerpt hash. complete means the model, amount and unit can be checked in the excerpt. partial means one or more required elements cannot be checked there. unavailable means historical evidence cannot be recovered. A summary, excerpt and official page support different levels of verification.</p>
    <h2>4. Generated summaries</h2><p>Some observation summaries are generated by an LLM and marked summaryOrigin=llm. They can be wrong. Follow the stable record ID, structured fact, saved excerpt and official page to verify a claim. API and RSS summaries disclose this origin.</p>
    <h2>5. Conditions before comparison</h2><p>Each record retains the precise amount, original currency, unit quantity and unit name, input/output/cache component, region, service tier, billing mode, context band and time condition. We do not convert currencies or select a lowest price across incompatible conditions on the English pricing pages. Raw condition values remain visible. A source that does not specify a condition separately has not established that no restriction exists.</p>
    <h2>6. Supplemental datasets and availability</h2><p>Third-party usage rankings and manually maintained exchange rates or capability lists have separate update schedules. The Chinese cost calculator and compute market references are supplemental datasets. Unknown information stays unknown. Overseas registration, payment and API availability have not been verified; an English page does not establish those capabilities.</p>
    <h2>7. Freshness and failed updates</h2><p>A successful download, a validated price parse and the last accepted fact are different signals. fresh means the latest collection succeeded. stale means an update failed and previous accepted data is retained, with its last successful time where available. unknown means the update state is unknown. Evidence completeness is a separate dimension.</p>
    <h2>8. Revisions, withdrawals and caches</h2><p>Records retain stable identities and revision history. Withdrawn records remain reachable with their status. RSS is a static projection; already cached withdrawn entries cannot reliably be recalled. Record pages and API responses are the authoritative current state. Read the <a href="/changelog/">interface changelog (Chinese)</a> for contract changes.</p>
    <h2>Language defaults and privacy</h2><p>Only the homepage entry may choose a default language from a country lookup. Mainland China (CN) defaults to Chinese; other countries default to English. Your manual choice takes priority and is stored locally for 180 days. Deep links retain their language. If lookup fails, the homepage uses your browser's preferred language; without JavaScript it remains Chinese. A VPN or inaccurate country mapping can be corrected with the language links.</p><p>Country lookup uses a local database on our server and does not send visitor addresses to a new third-party lookup service. This product includes GeoLite2 country data created by <a href="https://www.maxmind.com/">MaxMind</a>, distributed via <a href="https://github.com/sapics/geoip-country">geoip-country</a>. Database attribution and licensing: <a href="https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite/eula">MaxMind GeoLite EULA</a> and <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Country mappings can be inaccurate or lag network changes.</p>
    <p>English and Chinese prices are rendered from the same integrity-checked release. English details currently cover selected models; other detail, evidence and report links are explicitly marked as Chinese.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
